ArchiveEntry "Level C certificate: exact V-dot identity (parametric)"

/*
 * Exact mechanism of the degree-4 Level-C Lyapunov certificate.
 * V = x'P_poly x, x=(de,w1,w2), with P_poly (deg<=4 entries) the
 * cleared-denominator Lyapunov solution. Along x' = A x with
 * A=[[0,1,-1],[-K,-D1,0],[K,0,b]] (D2=-b), the Lie derivative is
 *
 *   V' = 2*K*(D1-b)*(D1*b-K) * (de^2 + w1^2 + w2^2).
 *
 * On the Routh region (D1>b, K>D1*b): the scalar mu=2K(D1-b)(D1b-K) has
 * (D1-b)>0 and (D1b-K)<0, so mu<0 and V'<0 --- strictly, on ALL of Level C.
 * The "boundary degeneration" lives entirely in this scalar mu->0, NOT in P.
 *
 * This is the parametric, machine-checked core. (P_poly>0 on Routh holds and
 * is numerically verified, but its parametric minor-QE times out separately.)
 *
 * V' written out explicitly below; identity verified by QE.
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real D1; Real b; Real K; Real de; Real w1; Real w2;
End.

Problem
  \forall D1 \forall b \forall K \forall de \forall w1 \forall w2 (
      2*D1^2*K*b*de^2 + 2*D1^2*K*b*w1^2 + 2*D1^2*K*b*w2^2
    - 2*D1*K^2*de^2 - 2*D1*K^2*w1^2 - 2*D1*K^2*w2^2
    - 2*D1*K*b^2*de^2 - 2*D1*K*b^2*w1^2 - 2*D1*K*b^2*w2^2
    + 2*K^2*b*de^2 + 2*K^2*b*w1^2 + 2*K^2*b*w2^2
    = 2*K*(D1-b)*(D1*b-K)*(de^2 + w1^2 + w2^2)
  )
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  QE
End.

End.
